From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wu <wuwei.vip@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:23:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tvOS: run the iOS app on Apple TV

Build the iOS front end for tvOS: guard the APIs tvOS does not have (the
Files document picker and cloud saves, the shake and phone-gyro motion
sensors, haptics, screen brightness, the external-display scene accessory,
interface orientation, sigaltstack, Slider/Stepper and insetGrouped in the
SwiftUI launcher) with TARGET_OS_TV / os(tvOS), accept the appletvos
platform in stage_resources.sh, and drop IOKit from the iOS link line
(the tvOS SDK has no IOKit; nothing in the host links against it).

Verified on an AppleTV11,1 (A12, tvOS 26.6): the app builds, signs with a
free personal team, installs over a network-dev tunnel and launches; the
launcher runs with a controller. The game itself stops at the engine's
Metal 4 requirement (A12 has no Metal 4), which is a hardware limit, not
a porting gap: an M3-or-newer Apple TV should get past it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#868
Reason: a tvOS target for Apple TV: the iOS front end builds and runs on tvOS with these guards, which is the first slice of LNPANDY/NX2Apple#163 (the tvOS target and pipeline flags)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#163

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#868
Reason: TODO: why the fork carries this
Issue: TODO: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#<n>

